id: pm-ifuysd
title: Workspace snapshot heartbeat races atomic root activation and loses its writer lock
description: "A long restore renews the workspace writer lock under the tracker root while atomic activation renames and replaces that same root. A heartbeat write can race the swap, lose its temporary path with ENOENT, and fail an otherwise safe restore. Quiesce and verify the heartbeat before copying the current lease into staging and activating the staged root, while preserving TTL exclusion against competing writers."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-29T22:50:13.344Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-29T22:59:46.119Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-29T22:56:38.697Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-29T22:56:38.697Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: A restore longer than the lock TTL rejects a competing writer; heartbeat renewal cannot race the root swap; the staged root carries the verified current lease through activation; lock loss and malformed ownership still fail closed; focused snapshot tests and full coverage pass.
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: Quiesce heartbeat across the rename gap and resume it on the activated root before backup cleanup.
expected_result: Long snapshot activation retains exclusive writer ownership without racing lock-file atomic writes.
actual_result: "The verified current lease is copied into staging, activation occurs with no concurrent renewal against the renamed path, and renewal resumes on the stable active root."
